<http://data.silknow.org/object/1518a010-a585-3827-a537-da80ac1d328d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Evening dress made of black machine-made net on which is embroidered a crewel work pattern of flowers in blue, pink, green and yellow, and an interlaced scalloped edging in pink and yellow. With a low necked bodice of black satin with short sleeves, one of which retains its puffed and gathered black machine-made lace trimming and a V-shaped waist. It laces at the back and is lined with white cotton. Hand stitched. The skirt is of net and has a flounce embroidered on it, and two additional ones are attached.\n\nWith an additional bodice of black silk covered with embroidered net. Similar in shape to the bodice of the dress, but the point at the waist is not as deep. Lined with white cotton and fastens at the back with hooks. A pleated band has been detached from the bodice."@en , "Evening dress made of embroidered machine-made net, satin and lace, with an additional bodice and pleated band, England, ca. 1855"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/2e78eaac-25a3-3072-ba0d-5c540fb9c5e5> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b39dde1a-55ec-3a87-b719-d108a59f8861> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/3902c704-ae85-3f02-9c3a-2838e408d04d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e2d5de13-2e0d-301b-83b4-d27152b213d0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Evening dress made of embroidered machine-made net, satin and lace, with an additional bodice and pleated band, England, ca. 1855"@en , "Evening dress made of black machine-made net on which is embroidered a crewel work pattern of flowers in blue, pink, green and yellow, and an interlaced scalloped edging in pink and yellow. With a low necked bodice of black satin with short sleeves, one of which retains its puffed and gathered black machine-made lace trimming and a V-shaped waist. It laces at the back and is lined with white cotton. Hand stitched. The skirt is of net and has a flounce embroidered on it, and two additional ones are attached.\n\nWith an additional bodice of black silk covered with embroidered net. Similar in shape to the bodice of the dress, but the point at the waist is not as deep. Lined with white cotton and fastens at the back with hooks. A pleated band has been detached from the bodice."@en ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.312 to B-1965" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O316443> .

